From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Thu, 6 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: use duelist helpers in processor.cpp (part 1)

Part 1 is processor.cpp lines 1 to 2932 (before calculate_battle_damage).

Changed (same result with 2 duelists):
- 23 explicit pairs or statement groups became loops over n_duelists in the same order: shuffle_deck_check and shuffle_hand_check reset and shuffle (3 times each, 12 groups as 6 pairs of loops), infos.priorities reset (6), core.hint_timing set/and/or (3), battle damage on player 0 then 1 (2).
- 2 loops `p < 2` now use n_duelists.
- 6 checks `event_player == 0 || event_player == 1` now use is_duelist(event_player). event_player is a uint8_t, so the accept set is the same.
- 33 `1 - x` now use opponent_of(x). x is infos.turn_player, a check_player derived from it, or the triggering_player of a chain. All are 0 or 1 here and the result goes into uint8_t arguments, array indexes or an int32_t that holds 0 or 1.

Left unchanged: 2 `1 - priority` (decision needed), check_hint_timing self/opponent swap, hint_timing `||` read, std::array<bool,2> bd (needs header), PLAYER_NONE uses (phase 2), pre_field and flag[1] (not players). See unchanged-sites.md.
